 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to the accreditation of persons\nappointed as Indian police officers",
    "basePrintNo": "S8894",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8894-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §846-h, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8894\n\nSPONSOR: LITTLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to the accreditation of\npersons appointed as Indian police officers\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to include persons appointed as Indi-\nan police officers within the definition of the term \"law enforcement\nagency\" for the purposes of the law enforcement accreditation council.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 9 of section 846-h of the\nexecutive law, as amended by chapter 625 of the laws of 2005 to include\nIndian police officers in the definition of a \"law enforcement agency\"\nfor purposes of that section. The effect of the amendment is to allow\nIndian police officers to participate in the accreditation process\noffered by the Law Enforcement Agency Accreditation Council within the\nState's Division of Criminal Justice Services.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nPursuant to Executive Law § 846-h, many entities may participate in the\naccreditation process of the Law Enforcement Agency Accreditation Coun-\ncil.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nParticipation in the Accreditation Council program provides a voluntary\nopportunity to demonstrate that law enforcement meets model standards\ndeveloped by the Accreditation Council for operating policies, equip-\nment, and facilities. The program would assist in reviewing the effec-\ntiveness of its law enforcement services, thereby increasing public\nconfidence.\n\nThis bill includes Indian police officers within the definition of the\nterm \"law enforcement agency\" for the purposes of the law enforcement\naccreditation council.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2005 - S .5205 (LaValle) - Chapter 625 of the Laws of 2005\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
